  <name>bettershot</name>
  <summary>Capture a screenshot and annotate it</summary>

  <description>
    <p>
      bettershot captures a region, a window or a whole monitor and lets you
      mark it up straight away, then copy the result to the clipboard or save
      it to a file.
    </p>
    <p>Tools:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Arrows, lines, rectangles and ellipses</li>
      <li>Freehand brush and text</li>
      <li>Numbered markers for step-by-step walkthroughs</li>
      <li>Highlighting, and blur or pixelation for hiding sensitive details</li>
      <li>Cropping, with full undo and redo</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      It runs on Linux and Windows. Its annotation model is adapted from Satty,
      whose small and obvious toolset it deliberately follows.
    </p>
  </description>

  <launchable type="desktop-id">org.bettershot.Bettershot.desktop</launchable>

  <url type="homepage">https://github.com/bettershot/bettershot</url>
